# Explicit window suppression for test children

The combined test inventory contained 34 statically imported Node child-process
calls in 23 files without an explicit `windowsHide: true` option. An inert
execution of the exact staging boot function confirmed the omitted option;
it created no actual child or window. This change supplies the option after
other options, including spreads, without changing executable paths, arguments,
environment values, callbacks, test identities or expected results.

The added Node regression checks the declared test inventory and rejects
missing, false, overwritten and computed-key lookalike options. It recognizes
named and namespace imports, aliases and lexical shadowing. Its scope is
statically imported Node child-process APIs, not universal process observation.

Validation used the existing local runtime, without result-cache acceptance,
automatic retry or model grading:

- Final five guard cases: five passed, zero failed/skipped; native exit 0.
- The same final guard with the exact `e80a0ee984efcb91363c20956ab8a1b72bda8d37`
  parent inputs supplied in memory: four passed, one failed; native exit 1.
  The inventory case identifies all 34 omissions. No source file was rolled back.
- AST comparison before/after the 23-file edit found only the added options.
  Their raw hashes also match the saved source at
  `811f99c4b2711016c4b7caefd2a5eb1c007b8400`.
- TypeScript `--noEmit` passed. Gate classification passed for 1,517 files,
  including 188 Node files. These are inventory counts, not executed cases.
- Platform scan of all 24 changed executable paths found zero command hits.
  Whole-repository discovery separately failed with
  `platform-scan-discovery-incomplete`; no repository-wide clearance is claimed.
- Read-only whitespace validation with `core.whitespace=cr-at-eol` passed.
  The existing CRLF file retains its line endings; no Git setting was changed.

The source was preserved at the named immutable checkpoint and continued in
the single admitted combined checkout. Machine receipts retain the edit hashes,
parent-input control and native results under `fleet-briefs/routing-20261101/`
with the `lead-768-` prefix. One initial author invocation used an invalid
Windows `--import` spelling and failed before the guard; its output is retained
